   config.i18n.fallbacks = true
diff --git a/docs/deploy.md b/docs/deploy.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..03ee528
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deploy.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+## Deploy (one box)
+
+Fizzy ships a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) config for a single Linux server
+with Docker. SQLite, files, the web process, and background jobs run in one
+container. kamal-proxy terminates SSL. Data is stored on a Docker volume so it
+survives the next deploy.
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with [Docker](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) installed
+- DNS for your hostname pointing at that server (ports 80 and 443 open)
+- A container registry (Docker Hub, GHCR, …) you can push to
+- An SMTP server for magic-link login and notifications
+
+### Configure
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` and fill in:
+
+1. **Hostname** — `servers`, `proxy.host`, and `APP_HOST` (use the same public hostname)
+2. **Mail server** — `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USERNAME`, `SMTP_DOMAIN`, and `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`
+3. **Image / registry** — `image` and `registry.username` (and `registry.server` if you are not on Docker Hub)
+
+Edit `.kamal/secrets` and fill in:
+
+- `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD` — registry access token
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE` — generate with `bin/rails secret`
+- `SMTP_PASSWORD` — password for your SMTP server
+
+You can paste values directly or keep the `$ENV_VAR` form and export them in your shell.
+
+SSH user defaults to `root`. Uncomment `ssh.user` in `config/deploy.yml` if you log in as someone else.
+
+### Setup
+
+From your laptop, with SSH access to the server:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+That builds the image, installs kamal-proxy, obtains a Let's Encrypt certificate,
+and boots Fizzy. When it finishes, open `https://your-host`.
+
+Later deploys:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+SQLite databases and uploaded files live in the `fizzy_storage` volume and are
+left in place across deploys.
+
+### Jobs
+
+Background jobs run on the box inside the web container (Solid Queue in Puma).
+You do not need a separate jobs host for this setup.
+
+### Console
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal console
+bin/kamal logs
+bin/kamal shell
+```
